  "notes": [
    "creusot-std std::convert::Into trait declaration is an external specification boundary. Its generic method contract only carries the implementation postcondition; the existing blanket Into<U> for T where U: From<T> forwards to From exactly.",
    "The setter precondition applies conversion requirements only if the incoming builder is valid, then relays TryInto::try_into preconditions and, for reachable Err cases, Into::into preconditions. No Error: From<E> bound was introduced.",
    "The setters model exact branches in terms of TryInto and Into postconditions. Concrete source-level Error conversion semantics require the relevant Into/From implementation contract.",
    "Header and extension setter bodies remain open because actual HeaderMap::try_append and Extensions::insert have no usable contracts in this harness; their own VCs are not included."
